<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goto Shojiro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1838–1897</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goto Shojiro was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> of the Tosa domain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and a leading statesman of the Meiji era. Drawing on the ideas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakamoto-ryoma">Sakamoto Ryoma</a>, he persuaded his lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamauchi-toyoshige">Yamauchi Toyoshige</a> to urge the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-yoshinobu">Tokugawa Yoshinobu</a> to return power to the emperor, which Yoshinobu did in 1867. He later served in Meiji governments and helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/itagaki-taisuke">Itagaki Taisuke</a> found the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberal-party-uk">Liberal Party</a> in 1881.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goto-shojiro.jpg" alt="Goto Shojiro" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goto_Shojiro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
